+/// Which move-time immobilizer aborted an action. See `Instruction::MoveImmobilized`.
+///
+/// EXACTLY the gen3 immobilizers that produce an EMPTY delta and are rolled inside
+/// `generate_instructions_from_existing_status_conditions`. Sleep, freeze, flinch,
+/// Taunt, Disable and recharge are all deliberately absent: each already leaves a
+/// distinguishable delta or is short-circuited in `cannot_use_move` before this
+/// function runs, so the renderer can already name them. A variant nothing emits is
+/// an untested branch in every match over this instruction.
+#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Clone, Copy)]
+pub enum ImmobilizeReason {
+    /// Showdown gen3 `attract.onBeforeMove` returned false: `|cant|<ident>|Attract`.
+    Attract,
+    /// Showdown gen3 `par.onBeforeMove` lost its 1-in-4 roll: `|cant|<ident>|par`.
+    ///
+    /// This one replaces a GUESS rather than a refusal. The renderer used to infer
+    /// `|cant|..|par|` from an empty tail on a probability-mass argument, with its
+    /// own comment conceding "a real miss renders identically". With the marker the
+    /// line is a fact, and -- the half that actually reduces fallback -- an UNMARKED
+    /// empty tail is now provably not an immobilization at all.
+    Paralysis,
 }
 
